## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/font.html
- Summary (EN): The Font node adds text to a layer by drawing Type 1, TrueType, or OpenType fonts into it. It supports any Unicode glyph and can output the result as a mask or a signed distance field.
- Résumé (FR) : Le nœud Font dessine du texte Unicode dans une couche, sous forme de masque ou de champ de distance signée.

- Inputs meaning: ["size_ref: representative layer that sets the output image size and controls the metadata"]

- Key parameters: ["Space: Image (layer image space, 0,0 at the display window center) or World (text placed in the X/Y plane with the 3D transform applied)", "Font: typeface; system fonts are listed automatically and other font files can be browsed", "Text: string to generate", "Output Type: Mask (rasterized mask) or SDF (signed distance field)", "Smoothing with Units and Width: softens jagged edges, in image-space units or pixels", "Horizontal Alignment and Vertical Alignment: position relative to the origin (Left, Center, Right, Top, Middle, Bottom and similar); Include Descender in Vertical Alignment moves the baseline to the descender", "Font Size: base size; Scale is applied on top of it", "Translate and Rotate Z: position and rotation around the world Z axis", "Tracking and Leading: horizontal and vertical character spacing; Leading only has an effect with multiple lines", "Oblique Angle: slant in degrees", "Level of Detail: number of points used in polygonal fonts"]

- Caveats: ["The text stays in world space even when size_ref is in a different space", "Leading has no effect on single-line text", "The available fonts depend on what is installed on the system"]

